attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a long spine.** Columns 0 to 19, `oxyR` to `metF`, are carried by 95 to 100% of chromosomes, all persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0 to 3% of calls {S1}. The model names 89 to 100% of them, fewest at column 1, `argH`, 89% {S1}.

@variable **A single variable column breaks the first spine**: column 20, carried by 63%, the most plastic stretch of the window {S2.c20, P}. Then columns 21 to 46, `metL` to `fieF`, are [[methionine and glycerol metabolism]], carried by 95 to 99% {S3, Q}. Through columns 47 to 54 a branch of 8 shell families runs in 11 to 13%, [[phage tail assembly]] {S4.b47, Q}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine columns than on the fork and variable ones**, 97 against 90%, and hesitates less there, 0.15 against 0.41 bits {M}. It hesitates most at column 79, `yihT`, a fork column, 0.68 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends in the `rha` and `frv` genes**, columns 53 to 63, [[rhamnose and fructose transport]] {S4.c53-59, S4.c60-63, Q}. The last column is `yihT`, in 31% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 94% of genes**, 0.26 bits on average, perplexity 1.3 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 0.85 against 0.16 bits, and names fewer genes, 80% against 96% {C}.

